00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.790
- YouTube, I often talk
about how my mom crushed it.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.630
You know, I talked about writing

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.246
a book called Perfectly Parented.

00:00:05.246 --> 00:00:07.350
You're about to watch a video

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.250
that talks about that in detail.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.430
But ultimately, I believe
the biggest miss in the world

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:14.540
is people focusing on
things that don't matter

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.380
and underestimating things that matter.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.230
The story may confuse many,
but at the end of the day,

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:21.100
focusing on the things that matter most

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.170
and building up self esteem around that.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:27.730
And then suffocating and muting
the stuff society values,

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.550
because in reality long term,
it doesn't matter as much.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.800
That nuance, landing that plane is

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.423
what my mom did phenomenally.

00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:38.280
Watch this.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.920
- You're so confident
and so sure of yourself,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.160
but when you were just
starting, who was the person?

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:43.250
- My mom.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.083
- Your mom

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:44.916
- My mom.

00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:45.920
- What'd she do for you.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.520
- When I was nine years
old and opened the door

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
for an elderly woman at a McDonald's.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.330
She reacted as if I won
the Nobel Peace Prize.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.460
(audience laughs)

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.293
- Good mom.

00:00:56.293 --> 00:00:57.910
- What my mom did was super-smart.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.660
She overreacted on a
everything that I was doing,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.410
that was a good human trait,
and she held me accountable

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.200
for things that didn't matter like grades.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.040
My mom built huge self esteem in me,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.830
and I feel like the biggest
reason I am who I am today

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.130
to everybody, is coz I feel so guilty,

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.770
and so grateful for what she did for me.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.400
That I want to do it for everybody else,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.850
which is, guess what?

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:24.390
You suck at a ton (alarm beeps)

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:26.330
Good, so does everybody else.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.690
You're also probably pretty
(alarm beeps) rad at something.

